WEBVTT

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.560
All right... Just a little more, okay?

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.860
Okay, Haruka-neesama.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.240
Is it too tight for you?

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.420
No, it's fine...

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.670
There... I'm done, Chiaki!

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.510
How is it, Haruka-neesama?

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.630
It's cute, really cute!

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.860
Thank you very much, Haruka-neesama.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.020
It's finally a new year, right?

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.370
Yeah.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.410
Kana!

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.600
Didn't we agree to leave at seven o'clock?

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.920
We'll visit the shrine without you if you don't hurry!

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.320
I'm waking up, I'm waking up...

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.450
I'm waking up...

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.290
I'm waking up already...

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.120
But let me sleep just a bit longer...

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.630
I'm waking up now! Waking up now!

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.730
This is bad, I haven't prepared anything...

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:21.740
This is bad!

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.170
I have to hurry up!

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.280
Hey!

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.860
Uchida!

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.500
Happy New Year.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.830
Congratulations!

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.470
Sorry for the wait, Uchida.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.340
It's okay, it's okay...

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.620
Uchida, what's with all that excess baggage?

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.750
Chiaki, look at these. I bought all of it!

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:03.350
This is... a large serving given by the old men as a special bonus.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.350
Isn't that great?

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:08.180
Couldn't you have waited quietly?

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.360
Eh? But it's a festival...

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.750
No, you got it wrong.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.320
I understand... I understand you, Uchida!

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.780
Yeah! Just as expected of you, Kana-chan!

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.130
But Uchida, you forgot something important!

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.340
Fools seldom differ, huh?
But Uchida, you forgot something important!

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:20.780
But Uchida, you forgot something important!

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.600
Hey, Chiaki, how's yours?

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.800
Hey!

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.430
I see, I see!

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.460
H-Huh?!

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.560
Okay, I'll draw one too!

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.360
Geez, that girl...

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.000
How's your fortune for the year, Chiaki?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.610
Erm... It's all right.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.320
How is yours, Haruka-neesama?

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.840
It has good vibes.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.840
That's good to hear.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.580
Shall we go tie them?

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.400
Kana-chan! Kana-chan!

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.130
Can you lend me 100 yen?

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.210
Why, Uchida? Have you spent all your money?

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:23.260
Yeah...

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.430
Geez, you really are hopeless...

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.190
Here...

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.220
Thanks, Kana-chan!

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.770
H-Hey! Pay me back later!

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.330
Excuse me! Can I have a Fortune Slip please?

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:38.440
Okay!

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.250
Awesome!

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.670
Hey, Chiaki!

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.050
Look at this!

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.000
Chiaki!

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.380
I would like to have a Fortune Slip.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:24.140
What's up with that smile, Uchida?

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:26.370
Did you eat something weird?

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:30.120
My fortune for this year is great!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.050
Especially in romance!

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:42.090
Uchida, a prince is fictitious and doesn't exist in reality.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.200
He exists!

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:48.720
Uchida, a prince only exists in fiction, any resemblance to real life is purely coincidenta—

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.030
He exists, he exists!

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:54.190
Don't put down someone else's fortune just because you didn't get a good one!

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.350
What's the fuss about romance?

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.030
It seems her luck with romance wasn't very good...

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.830
Money is more important, money!

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.950
...and her luck with wealth seems to be decent.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:06.040
If you don't have luck with money, romance is not a bad choice too.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.630
Oh! I heard that from Marie Something-inette...

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.170
Wrong...

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:15.350
No matter what you say, it said the one I'm waiting for will come.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.430
He will come, for sure!

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:19.890
Surely he will!

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:23.620
The person you're awaiting will arrive very soon!

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.200
Huh? Right here?

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.360
Yeah.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.570
She's sitting formally in wait, huh?

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.820
My legs are numb...

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:43.200
That's too quick, you sat for a mere 30 seconds.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:48.330
But... Is that person really coming?

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.870
Listen carefully, Uchida.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.420
Starting now, the first person who enters is your destined partner.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:55.650
Eh? I have no choice?

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.640
This has been setup by God.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.270
God did?

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:00.820
Of course.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:02.340
Here he comes!

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.600
Coming!

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.380
Wh-What should I do, Kana-chan?!

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.030
He came... He really came!

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.480
You're annoying, Uchida.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.590
What should I do?!

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.020
You should just go home.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.570
Congratulations on a happy new year.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.040
Congratulations.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.660
So, Uchida...

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.030
So, you say...

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.350
Fujioka-kun is Chiaki's favourite... and well-

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.120
This has been decided by God, what can you do?
Fujioka-kun is Chiaki's favourite... and well-

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.510
This has been decided by God, what can you do?

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:33.290
Eh?!

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.180
Speaking of which, my luck with friends isn't very good.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:39.240
Give up on friendship! Work for the sake of love!

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:41.300
But...

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.110
Steal him!

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:49.060
Oh right, you haven't returned the money you borrowed from Kana for the fortune slip yet.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:51.480
Oh yeah, I haven't gotten my money back...

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:14.980
You said that you'd pay for the fortune telling earlier.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.210
I didn't say that!

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.460
This world is all about money.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:21.170
Come to think of it, my luck with money isn't very good either...

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:25.220
Do you consider paying your debt as not having luck with money?

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.600
I don't feel any luckier in romance either...

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:32.020
But in comparison, Chiaki is having good luck in romance.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.190
Is that romance?

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.830
So in conclusion, luck with money seems to double as romance as well.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.620
I don't agree...

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:45.550
It's money, it's all money...

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:21.980
There's a difference in wanting to eat fried noodles, and wanting to eat instant cup fried noodles!

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:24.130
Ah, I completely understand that!

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.290
They're completely different foods.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.970
That's right, Touma.

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:31.850
They might look just like fried noodles, but they aren't better or worse!

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:35.180
The Instant Cup Fried Noodles is a completely different food.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.040
I call this the Instant Cup Fried Noodles phenomenon.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.900
Instant Cup Fried Noodles phenomenon?

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:44.230
Yeah, it happens regularly in our daily lives.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.720
Eh? Everyday?

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.990
Can you give me an example of when this phenomenon happens?

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:51.920
For example, look at my teddy bear.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:55.870
Although it looks like a bear, it's not really a bear. It's something different.

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:58.830
It even has a name - Fujioka.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:06.920
It seems that my job...

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:10.310
It seems that my problems with Reiko-san too...

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:16.460
Chiaki, your uncle is talking to that bear.

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.510
Don't call it "that bear".

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.520
It's Fujioka.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:23.340
Hey, Chiaki, don't you think your uncle wants to talk to somebody?

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:26.610
What have you been listening to this whole time?

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:29.300
Fujioka is not a substitute for someone to talk to.

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:31.060
It is a bear for someone to talk to!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.780
You just told me not to call it a bear...

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:36.140
It's <i>the</i> Instant Cup Fried Noodles phenomenon!

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:38.580
<i>The</i> Instant Cup Fried Noodles phenomenon?

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:41.960
In short...

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:48.200
The Instant Cup Fried Noodles phenomenon is when you find visiting relatives as a big nuisance?

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:51.590
Wrong! Please don't say anything that makes it look bad!

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.570
What in the world did you hear?

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.850
It's really profound and I don't understand...

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:59.510
Geez, you sure are helpless..

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:03.560
I will explain again so please listen to me, you idiot.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:08.790
For example, I have a planner here...

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:12.920
Just what exactly are you reading?!

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:14.840
I'm reading the Peyangu Magazine!

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.760
I am not asking about that!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.580
But I really don't understand what you’re saying...

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.340
You can just go home!

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.350
We're home!

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:23.250
Oh, I'm tired...

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:25.320
Welcome back, Haruka-neesama.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.590
Excuse me for having intruded.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:28.760
Ah! Welcome, Touma.

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:30.620
Welcome back, you two.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:32.780
Uncle, you came already?

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:35.310
I was impatient to see all of you.

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:36.850
Eh? I don't really care...

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:43.520
It seems that I'm... I'm just...

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:45.200
Hey, Kana...

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.270
Here he goes again...

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.520
Excuse me, I'll be heading to the toilet... The toilet~

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.780
You don't need to announce that!
Excuse me, I'll be heading to the toilet... The toilet~

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:51.790
You don't need to announce that!

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:56.730
Chiaki, you should have at least made him some tea.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:58.540
I-I'm sorry...

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.060
It's okay, don't worry about me.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:02.160
But...

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:06.330
Oh, since I have some leaves from this year's first tea harvest, I'll prepare tea.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:08.490
Thanks, Haruka-chan.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:14.400
Well after that, the problems at work...

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:19.910
It seems that my problems at work are...

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:22.620
It seems that my problems with Reiko-san too...

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:25.810
Here you are, Uncle.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.950
Thanks, Haruka.

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:32.980
Oh, it's delicious!

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.740
The first harvest tea of the year is good...

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:38.100
As expected of Haruka-neesama.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:42.020
She cheered up the troublesome and incompetent Takeru immediately.

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:43.660
Wasn't that just a cup of tea?

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:52.390
I knew it!

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:53.780
What's the matter, Kana?

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:55.410
Haruka, you've mistaken it!

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:56.720
These are just old tea leaves.

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:15.840
The tea that Haruka-neesama prepared wasn't something inferior to one made with tea leaves of the first harvest.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.190
It's something else!

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:19.530
I see. I'm starting to understand this!

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:21.500
What's with that 'it's delicious'?

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.140
Takeru can't tell quality apart.

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:28.280
Well... I just felt that it tastes different from what I drink at home...

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:32.490
Although it's not the first harvest tea, this tea is different from the stuff you drink at home.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.190
Instant Cup Fried Noodles phenomenon!

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:34.960
Huh?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:42.850
Instant Cup Fried Noodles phenomenon!

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:45.350
Eh? Wh-What's with that?!

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:56.740
As I was saying, your homeroom teacher, Tanaka-sensei, is sick.

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:58.150
What about it?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:01.170
That's why I'll go in his stead.

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.170
Go where?

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:03.750
House visit.

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.200
Go where?

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.830
House visit.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:11.220
But why you, the Health Education teacher, Kumada-sensei?

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:14.090
That's because I know a lot about you, Chiaki.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.510
Eh? You're going to meet her?

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:22.070
Yep, Haruka-chan asked me to...

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:24.850
So I'm here to be your guardian for once.

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:26.250
Haruka-neesama...

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:29.920
I think it's better for an adult to do it.

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:34.760
Yep, because I'm everyone's guardian. Please leave it to me.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:37.880
But Takeru and I are not related.

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:40.240
We are related - you're my cousin.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:41.900
Please don't worry.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:45.950
I'll have a nice exchange of information between the school and this household.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:50.280
But that teacher is...

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.460
And what about hobbies?

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:57.800
Yes, I recently took up throwing darts.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:00.030
Well, I was talking about Chiaki's hobbies...

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.480
Oh, is that so?

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:04.890
You really know how to joke.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:08.370
What's with this situation.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:09.980
Yeah, I'm always like this.
What's with this situation.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.160
Yeah, I'm always like this.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:13.630
Hey, Kana, what's going on here?

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:19.390
Speaking of which, there are kids who accidentally call their teachers as their mothers, right?

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:20.740
It's a marriage interview.
Speaking of which, there are kids who accidentally call their teachers as their mothers, right?

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:22.820
Marriage interview?

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:24.140
It's a marriage interview.

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:25.330
Why?

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:28.610
Why, you ask? In this situation, it's the only possibility!

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:31.660
Oh dear...

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.210
What are your hobbies?

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.550
It's always been soccer since long ago...

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:45.340
I see... What league are you aiming for in the future?

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.560
Ah... Well...

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:54.000
Hey, Kana?

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.050
Hey, Kana?!

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.670
What the hell is it this time?

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:01.860
A marriage interview...

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:03.140
A marriage interview?

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:05.470
Yes, it's definitely one.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.010
Sensei, why did you come here?

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:13.550
Don't you have stuff like grades to discuss?

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.500
Grades?

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.120
Wasn't it a house visit?

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.150
Oh!

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:18.920
Did you forget?

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.500
O-Of course not!

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.020
Grades, right? Grades... Please hold on...

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:26.390
Geez...

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.640
Please look at this...

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:33.180
This is...?

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:35.570
The results of her physical examination...

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:39.440
Height... Weight...

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:43.110
Is she eating properly at home?

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:45.570
Compared to other kids, her scores are a little...

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:48.740
Go home!

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:21.660
Haruka, we're out of milk!

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:23.060
We need it for stew tonight, right?

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.710
Eh? What should we do?

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:26.920
Oh, let me go buy some then.

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.930
Sorry about that, Fujioka.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:42.960
What's wrong, Chiaki?

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:47.720
Haruka-neesama, Fujioka is missing!

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:51.110
Eh? I didn't see it though...

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:54.700
All right! Chiaki-chan, let your uncle help you find it.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:57.290
Oh, you're still around, Takeru?

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:58.590
Yes, I am.

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:02.290
Right,

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:05.660
the preparation's complete.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.580
What are you trying to do?

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:11.620
Listen, what you're looking for will be in the direction the pen falls towards.

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.640
What a fraud!

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:15.310
It's very accurate!

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:19.080
Here I go...

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.560
There!

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.440
It's pointing towards the kitchen.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.880
Can you cook this?

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.720
Hey, can you cook this?!

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:57.930
Can you eat this, Kana?!

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:59.800
Why are you asking me?

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:03.960
Who else would pull a prank like this?!

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.470
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.230
I'm sorry, I said...

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:09.210
See, it's accurate.

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:11.220
That's quite amazing!

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:14.330
Erm... I have something to find too...

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:15.230
What'd that be?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:18.280
It's nothing important...

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:20.190
Let's give it a shot anyway!

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.540
Here I go...

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:22.580
There!

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:34.260
Hey, Takeru, that's pointing to the veranda.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:38.680
I knew it... I knew it was you, Kana.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:39.810
What are you saying?

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:46.350
In the freezer's top shelf, right corner... That small but expensive ice-cream that cost nearly 300 yen...

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:48.770
You ate it!

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:50.970
Is there... Is there proof?!

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.400
Kana...

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:56.300
Where's your apology?!

00:20:56.300 --> 00:20:58.410
I'm sorry!

00:20:58.410 --> 00:20:59.970
What's the trick?

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:01.350
There isn't any.

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:02.200
There isn't?

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.540
I don't believe it!

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:06.890
Try searching for something then.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.500
You're right...

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:14.870
Let's try looking for my cool future husband!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.500
Okay!

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:18.640
Here I go...

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:19.970
There!

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:31.720
Oh, so my future husband lives in the heavens...

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.030
Huh? That's weird.

00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:36.240
What a waste of time.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:41.680
Coming!

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:51.530
Coming!

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.340
Here I am!

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:02.810
I'm back.

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:06.270
You're really slow, Fujioka.

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:07.610
Oh, sorry...

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:10.810
It was crowded at the store and I rushed back as fast as I could.

00:22:10.810 --> 00:22:14.430
I forgot which floor you lived on and went all the way to the rooftop.

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:15.460
The rooftop?

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:16.230
Yeah.

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.070
Wouldn't you normally realize before reaching the rooftop?

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:21.570
I was in a rush and got careless...

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:29.540
Really? How many times have you come up. You really are dumb.

00:22:29.540 --> 00:22:31.760
It's really embarrassing.

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:33.920
She didn't notice.

00:22:39.050 --> 00:22:41.760
This is the 108th time today.

00:22:49.770 --> 00:22:53.980
Again. I can't stand it. Again!

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:57.220
I have no choice. I'll tie it up and try again.

00:22:57.220 --> 00:22:59.370
Erm, sir?

00:22:59.370 --> 00:23:00.490
Yes?

00:23:00.490 --> 00:23:03.270
Can I close for today?

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:06.930
I understand. I'll be here tomorrow morning.

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:08.520
Sorry about that.

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:14.020
Fate isn't very straightforward, huh?

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:19.970
I'm okay with that, because it's through adversity that we understand true values.

00:23:20.590 --> 00:23:23.380
Wait for me, Minami Haruka!

00:23:31.310 --> 00:23:34.440
Speaking of which, Uchida really can eat.

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:36.150
The pot is calling the kettle black, huh?

00:23:36.150 --> 00:23:38.170
But the food at the stalls really is enticing.

00:23:38.170 --> 00:23:39.420
Even Haruka-neesama.

00:23:39.420 --> 00:23:41.660
Next time on Minami-ke Okaeri:

00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:42.330
Me Too.

00:23:42.330 --> 00:23:44.370
Kana, you haven't eaten enough?

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:46.250
That's not it!
